title: tests, and how to run them safely
pid: b097fec4-6e5a-4e12-b41f-20887995bbe4
body: |2-
  Rust tests are built as five binaries, 'tests/grouped_*.rs' (Cargo.toml says
  'autotests = false'); each 'tests/X.rs' is a module of one of them, and
  'tests/unit/X.rs' is compiled into the server library by a '#[path]'
  line in the module it tests.
  'tests/refresh/' is compiled into the library from 'server/refresh/mod.rs'. Mine:
  'bash/nextest.sh --lib' (refresh, 'tests/unit/heralds.rs', 'view_text_delta.rs');
  '--test grouped_views' ('content_view.rs', 'initial_view_bfs.rs', 'viewnode_ids.rs', ...);
  '--test grouped_overrides' ('what_the_refresh_keeps.rs', 'view_stats_sharing.rs');
  '--test grouped_repos' ('redraw_delta.rs', 'viewnode_id_stability.rs'). Run from the
  repo root; fixtures are copied to /tmp and no server starts. [[id:302fa5ad-d404-4bc2-861a-65742cb4aa1e][Tess]] (the tests) owns the harness.
  The other suites are safe beside the running servers too: 'bash/emacs-tests.sh'
  and 'bash/nvim-tests.sh' start none, and 'bash/integration-tests.sh' and the AI
  reader's 'python3 tools/skg-for-ai/test_skg_for_ai.py' run 'target/debug/skg' on
  ports of their own, so 'cargo build' first. The team's servers run 'target/release/skg'.
